<title>NETHERLANDS: Common Fund approves sugar project in Zimbabwe.</title>
<headline>Common Fund approves sugar project in Zimbabwe.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Common Fund for Commodities, a U.N. affiliate, said on Friday it had approved a grant of $630,000 to improve the efficiency of African sugar cane production.</p>
<p>The three-year project, submitted to the Fund by the London-based International Sugar Organization, will be piloted in Zimbabwe and will examine among other things co-cropping sweet sorghum with sugar cane, thereby utilising fallow land.</p>
<p>&quot;The technologies (developed in the project) will ultimately benefit smallholder farmers...planting sweet sorghum alternating with sugar cane,&quot; the Fund said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
